<title>UK: Rolls-Royce steam charges wipe out yr profits.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce steam charges wipe out yr profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)	    3.19 LOSS vs 10.25 PROFIT</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)     3.3		    vs 3.0</p>
<p> Total dividend pence) 5.3		   vs 5</p>
<p> Pretax		   28 LOSS     vs 175 PROFIT</p>
<p> Turnover	    4,291		  vs 3,597</p>
<p> Operating profit    126		    vs 155</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits before exceptional charges for the aero-engines and industrial power group of between 205 and 235 million stg against 143 million stg in 1995.</p>
<p>Exceptional charges in 1996 included 248 million pounds of provisions and write-offs to cover disposal of the steam power generation businesses.</p>
<p>Rolls said operating profits before inclusion of operations to be discontinued rose to 242 million stg from 178 million stg in 1995.</p>
<p>Full company name Rolls-Royce Plc</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
